# Prettier is the formatter of record for everything — code and docs alike. Import order is Biome's
# (`biome.jsonc`, which restates this file's code exclusions, since Biome does not read it).

# Binary / media — not text Prettier should touch.
**/*.png
**/*.jpg
**/*.jpeg
**/*.gif
**/*.svg
**/*.pdf
**/*.mp4
**/*.woff
**/*.woff2

# Auto-generated / vendored / build output — not ours to format.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/generated/
**/out/
**/target/
**/.turbo/
**/.cache/
**/coverage/
**/test-results/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Lockfiles — auto-generated; formatting corrupts them.
yarn.lock
package-lock.json
pnpm-lock.yaml
.yarn/

# Frozen eval corpus + recorded baseline — reformatting would break determinism.
eval/fixtures/
eval/baseline.recall.json

# Frozen turn replay fixtures — `slopweaver turn freeze` is their only writer, and it emits
# `JSON.stringify(…, null, 2)`. Prettier collapses short arrays onto one line, so formatting these makes
# every re-freeze a spurious diff and invites someone to hand-edit a redacted file instead of re-cutting it.
src/__tests__/fixtures/replay/

# Cross-project contract goldens — a vitest file snapshot is their only writer, compared BYTE for byte, and
# Prettier collapsing a short array would fail the producer test on a file nobody changed.
src/__tests__/fixtures/contract/

# Next.js build output for the local docs site.
**/.next/

# The redacted per-case answer-quality artifact — `slopweaver dev answer-quality --selftest --artifact` is its
# only writer, and it emits an unpadded markdown table. Prettier pads table cells to a common width, so
# formatting it makes every re-cut a spurious diff and stops the committed file from being what the verb
# actually produces.
eval/answer-quality-per-case.artifact.md
